from pathlib import Path
import shutil,hashlib,json,sys,platform,os,pickle,datetime,difflib
import numpy as np
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
O=Path('source://ftf1d')
R=O/'remediation/results/ftf1d-p2-full-20260919'
def sha(p):
 h=hashlib.sha256()
 with open(p,'rb') as f:
  for b in iter(lambda:f.read(1048576),b''):h.update(b)
 return h.hexdigest()
def write(p,v):p.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2,default=lambda x:x.tolist() if hasattr(x,'tolist') else str(x))+'\n')
(W/'.gitignore').write_text('__pycache__/\n*.pyc\nscratch/\n.mplconfig/\nruns/\n')
for d in ['source/src','source/experiments','figures','tables','scratch']:(W/d).mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
m=json.loads((O/'repair/implementation_manifest.json').read_text())
for f,h in m['files'].items():
 assert sha(O/'corrected_project'/f)==h
 shutil.copy2(O/'corrected_project'/f,W/'source'/f)
for f in ['TRAINING_MAP.md','experiments/reproducible.py','experiments/execution_worker.py','experiments/p2_core_benchmark.py']:
 shutil.copy2(O/'corrected_project'/f,W/'source'/f)
(W/'production.diff').write_text('# No production source differences; all 17 src files and TRAINING_MAP.md match frozen FTF-1D.\n')
write(W/'baseline_manifest.json',m)
inputs=[]
for ds in ['adult','bank','credit']:
 for trial in range(5):
  p=R/f'P2_{ds}_k10_t{trial}'
  b=pickle.load(open(p/'input.pkl','rb'));s=b['settings'];req=json.loads((p/'request.json').read_text())
  assert s['T']==15 and s['k']==10 and s['trial']==trial
  assert {str(c):list(map(int,x)) for c,x in b['removed'].items()}==req['removed']
  inputs.append(dict(dataset=ds,trial=trial,settings=s,input=str(p/'input.pkl'),input_sha256=sha(p/'input.pkl'),request=str(p/'request.json'),request_sha256=sha(p/'request.json'),spec_sha256=sha(p/'spec.json'),n=sum(map(len,b['client_data'].values())),d=next(iter(b['client_data'].values())).shape[1],clients=len(b['client_data']),removed=sum(map(len,b['removed'].values())),meta=b['meta']))
write(W/'input_manifest.json',inputs)
run='round-budget-'+datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ')
(W/'RUN_ID').write_text(run+'\n')
env=dict(python=sys.version,executable=sys.executable,numpy=np.__version__,platform=platform.platform(),machine=platform.machine(),cpu_count=os.cpu_count(),thread_settings={k:'1' for k in ['OMP_NUM_THREADS','OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS','MKL_NUM_THREADS','NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS','VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS']})
write(W/'environment.json',env)
extra={str(p):sha(p) for p in [O/'repair/requirements.lock',O/'remediation/evidence/corrected_map_gate.json',O/'corrected_project/TRAINING_MAP.md',Path('[private-path-omitted]'),Path('[private-path-omitted]')]}
write(W/'reference_hashes.json',extra)
seeds=sorted({x['settings']['seed'] for x in inputs})
(W/'PROTOCOL.md').write_text(f'''# Frozen round-budget protocol\n\nRun ID: `{run}`. Prepared before experimental execution.\n\n## Population and numerical contract\nAdult, Bank, Credit; k=10; T=0,1,2; original five P2 seeds {seeds}; original independent record deletion batches (Adult/Credit 30; Bank 45). All 15 bundles, requests, source identities and unchanged settings are bound by input_manifest.json. Read existing expanded inputs directly; no new data preprocessing, re-partition, request draw or archive restore. Persistent client IDs and retained row order are preserved by boolean masks. Accepted original request records map local indices to stable source identities. Existing historical local-index warning remains applicable; use corrected bundle/request pairs.\n\nFTF-1D-descriptor-v1 source SHA256 {m['code_sha256']}; map SHA256 {m['map_sha256']}. All 17 source modules copied byte-for-byte and verified. Numerical map in source/TRAINING_MAP.md: b=12; preserved dataset clip; gamma=0; L=6; no anchor Lloyd; exact integer N/S/SS; indexed binary64 centers; PCG64 keyed streams; exact ties and strict-majority fallback unchanged. Environment in environment.json uses existing Python 3.12.14 / NumPy 2.3.5 read-only. No package installation. Original accepted gate is source lineage only, not a newly run gate.\n\n## Reuse decision\nThe corrected T=15 raw records have indexed numerical trajectories but only aggregate phase2_server seconds. Neither a budget-specific total public-call timer nor missing per-round server times can be recovered. No prorating or old runtime reuse. Newly run budgets are complete calls at their own T.\n\n## Keys, correctness and repetitions\n45 dataset/seed/T settings; four methods (Fresh, Direct/none, Basic, Runner-up); 180 unique keys and 135 replay/fresh comparisons. Each setting first builds its own cache-enabled original-population checkpoint at matching T, then executes an untimed-for-reporting correctness pass for all four methods in separate processes. Compare full C0..CT bytes, final centers, all integer N/S/SS, and exact retained-population fairness fractions. Compare prefix witnesses also to original T=15 accepted fresh/replay outputs. T=0 has one initializer/final center witness and zero refinement-statistic rows; N=A=P=S=J=0 and rates undefined. Failure stops that setting's timed phase and remains recorded.\n\nAfter passing, four timing repetitions, each in a fresh process. Fixed cyclic method ordering uses offset (dataset_index+trial+T+repetition) mod 4; thus every method occupies each position once. Gate pass order uses the same offset with repetition=0. There is no performance-driven rerun, seed selection or tuning. Report within-key median seconds; four repetitions measure timing noise, not independent scientific trials. Across-seed summaries use exactly five seeds per dataset/T; all seed-level ratios and min/max retained.\n\n## Measured boundaries\nAlgorithm seconds: perf_counter around full train_full(build_cache=False) or unlearn call, including validation, internal encoding/materialization, allocations, primitive timing and witness-ready numerical results. Fresh does not construct replay point caches.\n\nPrimary E2E request seconds: contiguous elapsed wall time from opening frozen input bundle through retained-input materialization (same work for every method), loading budget-matched checkpoint for replay, explicit pre-call GC, algorithm call, construction of full exact numerical witness, and equal-schema JSON witness serialization/write. Input bundle contains original population and deletion batch; request parsing and retained allocation are charged symmetrically. Quality scoring, result verification, reporting metadata/receipt writes and checkpoint setup are outside this boundary and separately observed. Witness creation and GC are explicit additions to the corrected September19 E2E sum. Input hashing/source gate checks occur before request timing. Full source/bundle load remains warm-OS-cache, separate-process measurement. Input preprocessing and initial environment/import startup are not request costs. A separate process-startup-inclusive view adds parent-launch-to-worker-ready time; it is not network latency.\n\nOffline setup: build and persist a separate original-population checkpoint for every T, with input loading, cache-enabled algorithm and serialization times and bytes. Never charge this to Fresh request latency. No serialized replay output is claimed reusable as a subsequent checkpoint. Quality is the exact maximum of group-average nearest-center squared distances on fixed-point retained records; evaluate gate outputs and associate identical repeated witnesses with the exact gate score. Repeated quality evaluation is unnecessary for measured calls.\n\nPrimitive client/server, encoding, materialization, certificate, failed-assignment and fallback timers are retained. Nested timers overlap and must not be added as disjoint totals. Uninstrumented algorithm overhead is algorithm elapsed minus disjoint encoding/input/cache/client/server timers, where applicable. Ideal parallel-client estimate is existing sum of per-round max-client times plus server totals; excludes untimed overhead and all communication, and is kept separate from measured serial wall time. C0 still requires client summary/group-count communication and server initialization; no transport is measured.\n\n## Lock, load and storage\nAcquire exclusive fcntl.flock on /private/tmp/ftf_benchmark_20260926.lock across the checkpoint, correctness workers and four repetition workers for one setting. File descriptor stays open in orchestrator; never unlink lock. Release between settings and allow one second for the other queued experiment. One worker at a time; five numerical-library thread controls fixed to one. Capture load averages and top CPU process snapshot before/after each setting. Desktop load outside this lock remains uncontrolled. All files are local in this workspace; no manuscript edits, shared Git mutation or publication. Fresh run is resumable with unchanged manifest and code hashes; completed batch receipts are reused only after hash verification.\n\n## Planned reporting\nPlots connect independently rerun cumulative request budgets C0/C1/C2, not sums across separately executed settings, not sequential deletion service and not a proved Pareto frontier. One PDF per dataset with algorithm and E2E panels, four methods, mean coordinates and five-seed SD, plus seed traces. Tables: raw 720 timed observations, 180 median key rows, 135 paired rows, dataset/T/method summaries with paired means, total-time ratio, wins/losses, seed range and noise. Certificates: N survivor point-rounds, A attempts, P passes, S passes retained after same-round fallback, J failed assignments duplicated by fallback; P/A differs from S/N; assignment point-units=N-S+J. No pooling with whole-client Task B.\n''')
print(json.dumps(dict(workspace=str(W),run_id=run,seeds=seeds,inputs=len(inputs),source_verified=True)))
